<title>USA: Miller Industries Q1 pre-split shr rises.</title>
<headline>Miller Industries Q1 pre-split shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Thousands Except Per Share Data)</p>
<p>						   Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							   July 31</p>
<p>										%</p>
<p>						   1996	1995  Change</p>
<p> NET SALES			     $   42,606$   32,884     30%</p>
<p> NET INCOME				   2,470     1,384     78%</p>
<p>NET INCOME PER COMMON SHARE-</p>
<p>  PRIOR TO 2-FOR-1 SPLIT		   0.21	0.14     50%</p>
<p>NET INCOME PER COMMON SHARE-</p>
<p>  EFFECTED FOR TWO-FOR-ONE SPLIT	     0.10	0.07</p>
<p>WEIGHTED AVERAGE NUMBER OF COMMON</p>
<p>&amp; COMMON EQUIVALENT SHARES</p>
<p>  OUTSTANDING				23,620    20,182</p>
<p>Note: Miller Industries Inc said included in net sales were sales of Company-purchased truck chassis of $10.4 million in the three months ended July 31, 1996, as compared with $10.4 million in the same period in 1995. The company has declared a two-for-one stock split to be effective for stockholders of record Sept 16, 1996. Common and common equivalent shares disclosed here have been restated to reflect both the three-for-two stock split which was effected on April 12, 1996, and the two-for-one stock split which will become effective on Sept 16, 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York newsroom, (212) 859-1610</p>
